    "code_caution": "A zoning amendment, Ord. No. 881, was adopted on 2026-06-22 and is not yet in the online code. It was not read, so it may change these rules. Ask the Township.",
    "checks": [
      "The zoning code has no accessory dwelling unit, accessory apartment, in-law or ECHO provision. A code search for those words found nothing",
      "Each district may be used 'for the following purposes and no others' (390-11B to 390-18B). The residential districts list the single-family detached house, and SR2, SR3 and UR also the semidetached house",
      "A two-family detached dwelling (one unit wholly or partly over the other) is permitted by right only in SR3 and UR. It needs 12,000 sq ft per dwelling unit with public sewer and water, or one acre per unit without (390-17, 390-18)",
      "A dwelling unit may have 'no more than one kitchen' (390-6, dwelling unit)",
      "Not more than one building housing a principal use on a lot unless a development plan is approved by the Board of Supervisors (390-28)",
      "Accessory buildings: 20 ft high at most, not in a required front or side yard, at least 10 ft from the rear lot line (390-29A)",
      "Parking: 3 spaces per dwelling unit for residential uses, not counting garages (390-37Q(1))",
      "In AP a farm may have up to two dwelling units per 40 acres, and an existing farm building may be converted to a residence by special exception (390-12B(4), C(2))",
      "A building on the Historic Resources Map may be reused for a single-family house, or for homes above an office or shop, under the adaptive reuse rules (390-70)",
      "Undefined uses are a conditional use only in the GI district, so there is no unlisted-use path for a second unit on a house lot (390-71.2B)",
      "On a nonresidential lot, living quarters are permitted only for proprietors, watchmen, caretakers or similar employees (390-30B(2))",
      "In the Stonersville and Limekiln Rural Village Overlays, homes are permitted above a business or office ('dual use'): each unit at least 500 sq ft with a kitchen and private bath, at most two units per acre, and the owner or manager of the business lives in one of them (390-19B(10), 390-20B(10))",
      "For a building on the Historic Resources Map in AP, R, RC, SR0, SR1, SR2, SR3 and UR, the uses allowed in the NC district may be permitted by conditional use (390-70B(3)(b)). The NC use list was not read",
      "A detached garage must be at least 10 ft from a dwelling, with no side longer than 40 ft (390-29B(2))"
    ],
